From eea72169db69694370eca244ae10b4c13a838336 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haowen1993 <39072333+haowen1993@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:32:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(client): give card TEXT its own language preference,
 defaulting to Chinese
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Card text was keyed off the interface language, which made a Chinese sidecar
unreachable by construction: `SUPPORTED_LNGS` has no `zhs` (no chrome catalog
exists), so `ensureCardLocale` was only ever asked for `en/es/fr/de/it/pt/pl/ja`.

Adds the third independent axis, mirroring `artLanguage` and its rationale:

  - `language`      — interface chrome
  - `artLanguage`   — card art
  - `cardTextLanguage` — card name / Oracle text / type line   (this commit)

The three sets are not nested in any direction: Polish has a UI catalog and no
localized card text (MTGJSON carries zero Polish foreignData); Chinese has text
and art and no UI catalog. Coupling any two forces either a full chrome
translation or no Chinese cards.

Default is `"zhs"` rather than `"auto"` — and the reason is specific rather than
a taste call: `"auto"` resolves to the interface language, which is never
Chinese, so the default would leave the sidecar permanently unloaded. `"auto"`
remains a legal value for any player who wants card text to track the UI.

`resolveCardTextLanguage` is total and never-throwing (an unrecognized persisted
value falls back to the interface language), and the loaders already tolerate a
missing sidecar — `ensureCardLocale` resolves a 404 to an empty map and both
call sites fall back to English per field, so an unpublished locale degrades
rather than breaking a card.
